4,Full article: Cultural identities in folk dance: Tharu dance songs and indigenous modernity,https://www.tandfonline.com/doi/full/10.1080/23311983.2026.2630571,"Themes of place have long structured Tharu folk dances and songs, particularly narratives of dislocation (e.g. out‑migration from the Dang Valley) and Kamaiya bondage. Glassberg’s claim that history and place are inextricably intertwined illuminates how environmental value is mediated by memory and association (p. 179, as cited in Furlan, Citation2017, p. 40). Performances attach the community’s history to Dang, from which Dangaura Tharus relocated southward (Burhan migration), narrating anxiety, exodus and the sedimented traumas of feudal exploitation.","Tharu, Dangaura",Indo-European
